Hi Luciano,

One additional point regarding your suggestion about using Qiskit SDK:

I appreciate the recommendation. However, the observation I reported is
fundamentally about hardware behavior, not tooling. The anomalous fidelity
scaling — increasing from 85.2% (1x CX) to 91.2% (11x CX) — was observed on
real hardware with verifiable job IDs.

This behavior remains unexplained regardless of which SDK is used to submit
the circuit.

I would greatly appreciate if you could share the actual
measurement/fidelity results from your reproduction attempt, along with job
IDs — as that would allow a direct comparison with my data.

