@TsafrirA inputs only include execution options:
``` python
def quantum_program_to_0_1(program: QuantumProgram, options: ExecutorOptions) -> ParamsModel:
    ...
    return ParamsModel(
        quantum_program=QuantumProgramModel(shots=program.shots, items=model_items),
        options=asdict(options.execution),  # type: ignore[call-overload]
    )
```

@SamFerracin 
This is not (in my mind) a general behavior, but rather an artifact of v0_1 where all relevant options were in the execution options. This is no longer the case in v0_2 and the behavior there is different (and this is why I pointed out that the `experimental` attribute gets lost in the roundtrip). From a broader perspective, I think you want the converter to return exactly the same types as the ones that went into the other converter. So, if you have

```python
def quantum_program_to_0_1(program: QuantumProgram, options: ExecutorOptions) -> ParamsModel:
```

the inverse converter should return `ExecutorOptions` and not `ExecutionOptions`.
